{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:FluidDynamics.QAubinLions","@type":"LeanModule","name":"FluidDynamics.QAubinLions","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Archimedean","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.singularDim_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.singularDim_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-aubin-lions.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The limit is smooth off a singular set of Hausdorff dimension ≤ 1\n(the Caffarelli–Kohn–Nirenberg bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.energy_inequality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.energy_inequality","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-aubin-lions.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The limit satisfies the energy inequality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.converges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.converges","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-aubin-lions.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.convergenceGap_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.convergenceGap_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-aubin-lions.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Strong `L²` convergence along it: the gap is eventually arbitrarily\nsmall.  Non-negative because it is a squared norm. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.qSeq_tendsto_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.qSeq_tendsto_one","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-aubin-lions.lean#L76-L76","doc":"…and tends to `1`, which is the limit the conjecture is about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.qSeq_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.qSeq_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-aubin-lions.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The subsequence lies in the q-NS regime `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-aubin-lions.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QAubinLions","kind":"class","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-aubin-lions.lean#L36-L85","doc":"**Conjecture class** for `conj:q-aubin-lions`.\n\nEncodes the conjectural content as a Lean type-class so downstream\ntheorems can take `[QAubinLions …]` as an explicit hypothesis\n(AGENTS.md §3b-cond).\n\n**Rewritten 2026-08-30.**  The single field was\n\n    compactness_threshold : ∃ q_thresh : ℝ, q_thresh > 0\n\n— \"there exists a positive real\", a theorem of ordered fields,\ndischarged by `1`.  It asserted nothing about compactness, about\n`q → 1`, or about the solution family, and its docstring had holes\nwhere the symbols had been dropped (\"a compactness exponent  such\nthat for all  the solution family\").\n\nThe class is now **parametrised by the objects the conjecture is\nabout**, and each field is one clause of the `.md` conjecture:\n\n> *there exists a subsequence `qₙ → 1` such that `v_{qₙ} → v*`\n> weakly in `L²`; `v*` is a weak solution of Navier–Stokes,\n> satisfies the energy inequality, and is smooth off a singular set\n> of Hausdorff dimension ≤ 1.*\n\nThis does **not** prove the conjecture.  It makes assuming it mean\nsomething: every field is refutable by a wrong object, and the\nnegative controls below exhibit such objects.\n\n**Parameters.**  `qSeq` is the extracted subsequence `qₙ` of substrate\nparameters; `convergenceGap n` is `‖v_{qₙ} − v*‖²_{L²}`, the `L²` gap\nalong it; `energyLimit` and `energyInitial` are `‖v*‖²` and `‖v₀‖²`;\n`singularDim` is the Hausdorff dimension of the singular set of `v*`.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] §q-deformed Aubin--Lions lemma: compactness of the\nsolution family as q → 1, `conj:q-aubin-lions` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:q-aubin-lions","label":"conj:q-aubin-lions","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-aubin-lions.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}